    Because the opponent is unresponsive, the optimal move for Round 10 is the same as Round 1. The uncertainty regarding the total number of rounds (8 to 10) does not affect the calculation, as the payoff for Defecting dominates Cooperating in every possible future state.

By Defecting every round, I ensure the highest possible score given the circumstances (finishing with 8 to 10 points, whereas Cooperating would result in 0).
